    description: "PR #763 stamped meta.receiver='qualified' on rust.py's Strategy-1 scoped-call emit sites, but Type::new()/Type::try_from() calls that resolve via a SECOND path (var_types constructor / method_resolver suffix) remain unmarked — e.g. rodio Red::new<-5, Decoder::try_from<-3, FlacDecoder::new<-2. These are CORRECT resolutions (call site named the type), so they are false positives in the raw find_receiver_blind_magnets count, NOT harmful magnets (the durable INV-fahub gate correctly ignores them). Cosmetic measurement-precision only; INV-fahub satisfied regardless. Fix: find the second Type::new resolution path in rust.py and stamp receiver='qualified', matching PR #763. Deprioritized cosmetic follow-up split from WI-makiz."  # 68c2
