  message: "DONE — fixed in the merged PR (WI-fazaj). rust.py's method_resolver / bare-name scoped-call fallback (Strategy 1 missed) now stamps meta.receiver='qualified' when the call named its type (full_scoped_name set), mirroring PR #763's Strategy-1 sites, so a correct associated-function call (rodio Red::new / Decoder::try_from) is no longer counted as a receiver-blind magnet in the raw find_receiver_blind_magnets diagnostic.\n\nTESTABILITY NOTE (owner ruled pragma): the branch is reachable ONLY through the full cross-package survey method_resolver — verified unreachable across 8 isolated analyze_rust scenarios (cross-file, nested modules, use aliases, generics, ::new ambiguity, re-exports), which all bind via Strategy 1 and are already stamped. A minimal RED test therefore cannot reach the emit, and the added qualified-stamp branch would break the 100% coverage gate; per owner direction it carries `# pragma: no cover` with a justification comment. rust.py stays at 100% (smart-test scoped-coverage confirmed). Cosmetic measurement-precision only; INV-fahub satisfied throughout. Sub-item context: raw-count follow-up split from WI-makiz; not a WI-kivip fold sub-item."  # fe80
